00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:44.803
is happening.

00:07:44.803 --> 00:07:46.220
It's just going
to keep happening.

00:07:46.220 --> 00:07:49.850
I mean I'm starting with,
you see in the videos--

00:07:49.850 --> 00:07:53.210
these videos are real--

00:07:53.210 --> 00:07:55.620
you see it doesn't
stop happening.

00:07:55.620 --> 00:07:56.120
right.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:56.912
It keeps happening.

00:07:56.912 --> 00:07:59.810
So if I have no vapor in there
to begin with, well, then,

00:07:59.810 --> 00:08:02.920
OK, evaporation is
going to go like this.

00:08:02.920 --> 00:08:06.740
All right, maybe this
is time, it is time.

00:08:06.740 --> 00:08:09.760
And then-- so
that's evaporation.

00:08:09.760 --> 00:08:11.760
But then, at a certain
time, at a certain point,

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.480
I'm going to have enough
gas molecules, gas water

00:08:14.480 --> 00:08:15.710
molecules in there.

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:18.325
So it starts out
at 0, and they're

00:08:18.325 --> 00:08:20.450
going to build up in there,
and at a certain point,

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:21.240
you got that.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:21.740
Right.

00:08:21.740 --> 00:08:24.060
And so, this would
be condensation.

00:08:24.060 --> 00:08:24.560
OK.

00:08:24.560 --> 00:08:27.630
We're starting with the
basics, condensation.

00:08:27.630 --> 00:08:28.970
Right.

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:32.270
And then at a
certain point, they

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:37.985
reach what's called dynamic
equilibrium, dynamic eqm,

00:08:37.985 --> 00:08:39.260
eqm is equilibrium.

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:44.660
So the dynamic equilibrium
is really important,

00:08:44.660 --> 00:08:48.590
because what happens there
is nothing is stopping.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:49.820
It's not the thing stopped.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:52.220
You can see it in the videos.

00:08:52.220 --> 00:08:55.570
I found it online,
so it must be right.

00:08:55.570 --> 00:08:58.100
So like, you know,
it's continually going.

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.510
It's a dynamic process.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:02.090
It's a dynamic equilibrium,
but they are equal.

00:09:02.090 --> 00:09:06.110
That point that happens
in these containers,

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:08.460
you can measure the pressure.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:10.240
That is very important.

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:11.340
Right.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:13.680
Because it's exerting a
pressure on the container.

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:16.140
It's exerting a
pressure on the liquid.

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:17.220
Pressure.

00:09:17.220 --> 00:09:18.150
Atmosphere.

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:22.210
Pressure, inside of a closed
container, vapor pressure.

00:09:22.210 --> 00:09:23.130
P vapor.

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:30.383
That happens when you hit
that dynamic equilibrium.

00:09:30.383 --> 00:09:31.800
Now why am I telling
you all this?

00:09:31.800 --> 00:09:33.180
Well, the vapor
pressure is going

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:36.680
to be how we understand
phase change.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:39.300
And so-- and so--

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:43.590
you kind of get a sense already,
kind of get a sense already,

00:09:43.590 --> 00:09:46.950
that this is going
to be related--

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:53.860
this is related, you know,
this depends on the bonding.

00:09:53.860 --> 00:09:54.360
Right.

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:58.910
So I just told you that
water was really special.

00:09:58.910 --> 00:10:00.640
So that means that how it--

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:02.500
it's the bonding between
the water molecules

00:10:02.500 --> 00:10:05.860
and how often can it
get out of the liquid,

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:08.587
it's related to the bonding.

00:10:08.587 --> 00:10:11.210
Right.

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:14.670
So if you take molecules that
we talked about on Monday--

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:18.020
these are just from
Monday-- propane and butane,

00:10:18.020 --> 00:10:20.600
now you understand, right?

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:23.960
Why is there this difference in
the vapor pressure of protane--

00:10:23.960 --> 00:10:26.390
propane, and the vapor
pressure of butane?

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:27.830
Well, it's how
they bond together.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:29.390
And you know exactly why.

00:10:29.390 --> 00:10:33.050
Because these are only
able to do [INAUDIBLE]..

00:10:33.050 --> 00:10:34.160
And so, this has a--

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.810
has a higher surface area.

00:10:35.810 --> 00:10:38.030
We talk about this in
terms of the boiling point,

00:10:38.030 --> 00:10:40.580
remember, as a proxy for
the intermolecular bonding

00:10:40.580 --> 00:10:41.200
strength.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:43.732
And now I'm giving you
the vapor pressure.

00:10:43.732 --> 00:10:46.190
So this is the vapor pressure
of these things is different.

00:10:46.190 --> 00:10:49.250
Those are measured-- those
