00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.450
what temperature is.

00:16:18.450 --> 00:16:21.870
See, the vapor
pressure is really

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:26.460
a link between
temperature and boiling.

00:16:26.460 --> 00:16:29.580
It's the length that you need to
understand between temperature

00:16:29.580 --> 00:16:30.930
and boiling.

00:16:30.930 --> 00:16:34.530
The reason why-- when you
increase the temperature

00:16:34.530 --> 00:16:36.600
of the water, the
reason why it boils

00:16:36.600 --> 00:16:40.020
is because you change
its vapor pressure.

00:16:40.020 --> 00:16:41.550
That's why it boils.

00:16:41.550 --> 00:16:43.110
That's what boiling is.

00:16:43.110 --> 00:16:43.610
OK.

00:16:43.610 --> 00:16:47.550
It's when you get it above
the atmospheric pressure.

00:16:47.550 --> 00:16:48.050
No.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:52.490
OK.

00:16:52.490 --> 00:16:55.090
So the-- so we got--

00:16:55.090 --> 00:16:57.580
OK-- so are we--
where-- there we go--

00:16:57.580 --> 00:17:00.230
we'll come to that in a minute.

00:17:00.230 --> 00:17:03.970
So if I were to plot
now, the vapor pressure--

00:17:03.970 --> 00:17:05.770
let's do this carefully here.

00:17:05.770 --> 00:17:06.760
OK.

00:17:06.760 --> 00:17:13.000
I'm going to make a plot of
